185
00:15:11,081 --> 00:15:18,160
Now here's a modern pocket camera with 12 megapixels of resolution, 36 times the amount

186
00:15:18,161 --> 00:15:24,080
in a package one fraction the size as a physical device.

187
00:15:24,081 --> 00:15:32,540
Perhaps the most groundbreaking of the digital entertainment products is the video game.

188
00:15:32,541 --> 00:15:36,040
The Wii became the must-have system in 2006.

189
00:15:36,041 --> 00:15:39,200
What was that?

190
00:15:39,201 --> 00:15:42,040
That was you missing.

191
00:15:42,041 --> 00:15:46,460
The key to the Wii's popularity is that it enables your body to interact with a video

192
00:15:46,461 --> 00:15:47,460
screen.

193
00:15:47,461 --> 00:15:53,220
Oh, not again!

194
00:15:53,221 --> 00:15:58,560
A company called Analog Devices designed the tiny digital motion sensor that is inside

195
00:15:58,561 --> 00:16:03,560
this handheld controller called a Wiimote.

196
00:16:03,561 --> 00:16:07,020
It's basically a mass that's suspended by some springs.

197
00:16:07,021 --> 00:16:11,920
So think about a trampoline, for example, that's suspended by springs in its periphery.

198
00:16:11,921 --> 00:16:16,060
Now the trampoline is capable of moving up and down in this direction, but it's also

199
00:16:16,061 --> 00:16:19,500
capable of moving left, right, or fore-aft.

200
00:16:19,501 --> 00:16:24,860
And that gets translated into a bitstream of ones and zeros, radio signals from the Wiimote

201
00:16:24,861 --> 00:16:28,480
over to the console.

202
00:16:28,481 --> 00:16:34,540
These sensors send data to a processor a hundred times more powerful than the personal computers of the early 1980s.

203
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:37,480
The Wiimote is going to take the output from our sensor,

204
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:43,680
and it's going to process it digitally and send it via radio wave to the game console.

205
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:48,760
And from the game console, it's going to process all of that information and output it to the video display.

206
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:53,220
There's millions and millions of numbers being calculated right now

207
00:16:53,221 --> 00:16:56,640
between what my Wiimote is sending for a radio signal

208
00:16:56,641 --> 00:17:01,740
and what the video game is actually doing in terms of placement of the ball

209
00:17:01,741 --> 00:17:05,060
and whether I've won, lost, hit it out of bounds, or kept it in bounds.

210
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:09,660
Of course, television went digital in the last generation, too.

